          skills21stCentury: "Critical Thinking:\n• As learners brainstorm in analysing the positive and negative impacts of robots on society.\n• Learners make deductions from their research when publishing their articles.\n\nCollaboration:\n• Sit in groups and take turns relaying their thoughts to their peers. The right ambience should be created to allow every learner to collaborate with others, building on points raised and putting down their collective observations while amicably resolving issues of differences in opinions.\n• Learners sit in groups and take turns relaying their thoughts to their peers. The right ambience should be created to allow every learner to collaborate with others, building on points raised and putting down their collective observations while amicably resolving issues of differences in opinions.\n\nCommunication:\n• Learners express their thoughts among their peers in an environment that is unbiased and free from fear or intimidation, and they patiently listen to others.\n• Learners contribute to the global discussion on these topics, expressing their thoughts in written form for a wider audience to read.\n\nLeadership: As learners sit in groups and brainstorm, they create and share tasks and responsibilities among themselves to achieve set goals for the group.\n\nCritical Thinking: As learners brainstorm in analysing the cost-benefit analysis and finding plausible use cases for robots in society/industry.\n\nInitiative: Learners are given the opportunity to write on a topic they deem important to them in this area, sharing their thoughts with the world.\n\nMedia Literacy: Learners have the opportunity to conduct a detailed literature review, analysing other people's works in the area they select.\n\nEmotional Intelligence: Learners develop the discipline of meeting deadlines and set objectives.\n\nInitiative: Learners are given the opportunity to research job postings they think are related to robotics.\n\nMedia Literacy: Learners have the opportunity to conduct a detailed review of each posting, analysing the requirements and job responsibilities.\n\nCritical Thinking: Learners make deductions from their research into what they think guarantees them consideration by an employer.\n\nCommunication: Learners learn to prepare written CVs and share the results of their research with their colleagues, justifying any points made.\n\nEmotional Intelligence: Learners develop the discipline of meeting deadlines and set objectives.",
